      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author combines explicit Hermite-product identities for rational KP wave functions with Calogero-Moser/bispectral data, then uses the zero-band condition to force nilpotent matrix data and identify an exceptional Hermite family indexed by a partition. The complete wave-function, integral and matrix-polynomial machinery is retained. Scalar-product, almost-biorthogonality and matrix examples are support, not independently counted.",
